{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Weighted Conformal Prediction under Prompt Shift\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research direction — Step 3 of the plan**\n",
    "\n",
    "We test the weighted CP pipeline proposed in §5.2 of the report.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Setup\n",
    "Since we only have logits from a single prompt variant (`base_icl1`), we simulate\n",
    "cross-prompt shift by treating the two halves of the 100-sample dataset as coming\n",
    "from two different prompt distributions:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Calibration half** ("prompt A") → used to compute nonconformity scores\n",
    "- **Test half** ("prompt B") → evaluated under the prediction sets\n",
    "\n",
    "The density ratio $w(x) = dP_{k_\\text{test}}/dP_{k_\\text{cal}}(x)$ is estimated\n",
    "via logistic regression on softmax probability vectors (the feature space available\n",
    "from our logits).\n",
    "\n",
    "### What we compare\n",
    "| Method | Quantile | Assumption |\n",
    "|--------|----------|------------|\n",
    "| Standard split CP | Uniform empirical | Exchangeability (same prompt) |\n",
    "| **Weighted split CP** | Weighted by $\\hat{w}(x)$ | Covariate shift OK |\n",
    "\n",
    "Target: $\\alpha = 0.1$, so coverage $\\geq 90\\%$ is the goal."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys, os\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, os.path.abspath('..'))\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.patches as mpatches\n",
    "\n",
    "from utils.weighted_cp import run_comparison, load_all_pairs, standard_cp, weighted_cp\n",
    "\n",
    "OUT_DIR  = '../outputs_kaggle'\n",
    "DATA_DIR = '../data'\n",
    "ALPHA    = 0.1\n",
    "\n",
    "MODELS = [\n",
    "    'qwen3-0.6b',\n",
    "    'qwen2.5-3b',\n",
    "    'qwen2.5-7b',\n",
    "    'olmo-1b',\n",
    "    'olmo-7b',\n",
    "]\n",
    "DATASETS = [\n",
    "    'mmlu_10k',\n",
    "    'hellaswag_10k',\n",
    "    'cosmosqa_10k',\n",
    "    'halu_dialogue',\n",
    "    'halu_summarization',\n",
    "]\n",
    "DS_LABELS = {\n",
    "    'mmlu_10k':           'MMLU',\n",
    "    'hellaswag_10k':      'HellaSwag',\n",
    "    'cosmosqa_10k':       'CosmosQA',\n",
    "    'halu_dialogue':      'HaluDial',\n",
    "    'halu_summarization': 'HaluSum',\n",
    "}\n",
    "MODEL_LABELS = {\n",
    "    'qwen3-0.6b':  'Qwen3-0.6B',\n",
    "    'qwen2.5-3b':  'Qwen2.5-3B',\n",
    "    'qwen2.5-7b':  'Qwen2.5-7B',\n",
    "    'olmo-1b':     'OLMo-1B',\n",
    "    'olmo-7b':     'OLMo-7B',\n",
    "}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1 — Run experiment: Standard CP vs Weighted CP"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "results = run_comparison(MODELS, DATASETS, OUT_DIR, DATA_DIR, alpha=ALPHA)\n",
    "print('Done. Models processed:', list(results.keys()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2 — Coverage and Set Size Table"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rows = []\n",
    "for short in MODELS:\n",
    "    for ds in DATASETS:\n",
    "        if ds not in results.get(short, {}):\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        r = results[short][ds]\n",
    "        rows.append({\n",
    "            'Model':    MODEL_LABELS[short],\n",
    "            'Dataset':  DS_LABELS[ds],\n",
    "            'CR_std':   round(r['standard']['coverage'] * 100, 1),\n",
    "            'SS_std':   round(r['standard']['avg_size'], 2),\n",
    "            'CR_wcp':   round(r['weighted']['coverage'] * 100, 1),\n",
    "            'SS_wcp':   round(r['weighted']['avg_size'], 2),\n",
    "            'n_cal':    r['n_cal'],\n",
    "            'n_test':   r['n_test'],\n",
    "        })\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "print(f'Target coverage: {(1-ALPHA)*100:.0f}%')\n",
    "df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3 — Coverage comparison: Standard vs Weighted"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 5, figsize=(18, 4), sharey=True)\n",
    "x = np.arange(len(MODELS))\n",
    "w = 0.35\n",
    "colors_std = '#4878CF'\n",
    "colors_wcp = '#D65F5F'\n",
    "\n",
    "for j, ds in enumerate(DATASETS):\n",
    "    ax = axes[j]\n",
    "    cr_std = [results[m][ds]['standard']['coverage'] * 100 if ds in results.get(m, {}) else np.nan for m in MODELS]\n",
    "    cr_wcp = [results[m][ds]['weighted']['coverage'] * 100 if ds in results.get(m, {}) else np.nan for m in MODELS]\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.bar(x - w/2, cr_std, w, color=colors_std, alpha=0.85, label='Standard CP')\n",
    "    ax.bar(x + w/2, cr_wcp, w, color=colors_wcp, alpha=0.85, label='Weighted CP')\n",
    "    ax.axhline(90, color='black', lw=1.2, ls='--', label='90% target')\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.set_title(DS_LABELS[ds], fontsize=11)\n",
    "    ax.set_xticks(x)\n",
    "    ax.set_xticklabels([MODEL_LABELS[m].replace('Qwen', 'Q').replace('OLMo', 'O') for m in MODELS],\n",
    "                       rotation=30, ha='right', fontsize=8)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylim(50, 105)\n",
    "    if j == 0:\n",
    "        ax.set_ylabel('Coverage Rate (%)')\n",
    "\n",
    "handles = [\n",
    "    mpatches.Patch(color=colors_std, alpha=0.85, label='Standard CP'),\n",
    "    mpatches.Patch(color=colors_wcp, alpha=0.85, label='Weighted CP'),\n",
    "    plt.Line2D([0], [0], color='black', ls='--', lw=1.2, label='90% target'),\n",
    "]\n",
    "fig.legend(handles=handles, loc='lower center', ncol=3, fontsize=10, bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.05))\n",
    "fig.suptitle('Coverage Rate: Standard CP vs Weighted CP ($\\\\alpha=0.1$)', fontsize=13, y=1.02)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('../figures_kaggle/fig_wcp_coverage.pdf', bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print('Saved fig_wcp_coverage.pdf')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4 — Set Size comparison"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 5, figsize=(18, 4), sharey=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "for j, ds in enumerate(DATASETS):\n",
    "    ax = axes[j]\n",
    "    ss_std = [results[m][ds]['standard']['avg_size'] if ds in results.get(m, {}) else np.nan for m in MODELS]\n",
    "    ss_wcp = [results[m][ds]['weighted']['avg_size'] if ds in results.get(m, {}) else np.nan for m in MODELS]\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.bar(x - w/2, ss_std, w, color=colors_std, alpha=0.85, label='Standard CP')\n",
    "    ax.bar(x + w/2, ss_wcp, w, color=colors_wcp, alpha=0.85, label='Weighted CP')\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.set_title(DS_LABELS[ds], fontsize=11)\n",
    "    ax.set_xticks(x)\n",
    "    ax.set_xticklabels([MODEL_LABELS[m].replace('Qwen', 'Q').replace('OLMo', 'O') for m in MODELS],\n",
    "                       rotation=30, ha='right', fontsize=8)\n",
    "    if j == 0:\n",
    "        ax.set_ylabel('Average Set Size')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.legend(handles=handles[:2], loc='lower center', ncol=2, fontsize=10, bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.05))\n",
    "fig.suptitle('Average Set Size: Standard CP vs Weighted CP', fontsize=13, y=1.02)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('../figures_kaggle/fig_wcp_setsize.pdf', bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print('Saved fig_wcp_setsize.pdf')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5 — Detailed: Coverage gap (Weighted − Standard)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gap_matrix = np.full((len(MODELS), len(DATASETS)), np.nan)\n",
    "for i, short in enumerate(MODELS):\n",
    "    for j, ds in enumerate(DATASETS):\n",
    "        if ds in results.get(short, {}):\n",
    "            cr_wcp = results[short][ds]['weighted']['coverage'] * 100\n",
    "            cr_std = results[short][ds]['standard']['coverage'] * 100\n",
    "            gap_matrix[i, j] = cr_wcp - cr_std\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "im = ax.imshow(gap_matrix, cmap='RdYlGn', vmin=-20, vmax=20, aspect='auto')\n",
    "plt.colorbar(im, ax=ax, label='Coverage gap: Weighted − Standard (%)')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(range(len(DATASETS)))\n",
    "ax.set_xticklabels([DS_LABELS[d] for d in DATASETS], rotation=20, ha='right')\n",
    "ax.set_yticks(range(len(MODELS)))\n",
    "ax.set_yticklabels([MODEL_LABELS[m] for m in MODELS])\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(len(MODELS)):\n",
    "    for j in range(len(DATASETS)):\n",
    "        v = gap_matrix[i, j]\n",
    "        if not np.isnan(v):\n",
    "            ax.text(j, i, f'{v:+.1f}', ha='center', va='center', fontsize=9,\n",
    "                    color='black' if abs(v) < 15 else 'white')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title('Coverage gain from weighted CP (positive = weighted is better)', fontsize=11)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('../figures_kaggle/fig_wcp_gap_heatmap.pdf', bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print('Saved fig_wcp_gap_heatmap.pdf')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6 — Inspect estimated weights for one (model, dataset)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pick Qwen2.5-7B on HaluDial — the hardest case\n",
    "short, ds = 'qwen2.5-7b', 'halu_dialogue'\n",
    "from utils.weighted_cp import load_all_pairs, estimate_weights\n",
    "from utils.weighted_cp import _softmax\n",
    "\n",
    "paired = load_all_pairs(short, ds, OUT_DIR, DATA_DIR)\n",
    "n_cal  = len(paired) // 2\n",
    "cal_pairs  = paired[:n_cal]\n",
    "test_pairs = paired[n_cal:]\n",
    "\n",
    "cal_feat  = np.array([_softmax(r['logits_options']) for _, r in cal_pairs])\n",
    "test_feat = np.array([_softmax(r['logits_options']) for _, r in test_pairs])\n",
    "w = estimate_weights(cal_feat, test_feat)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 3))\n",
    "ax.hist(w, bins=20, color='steelblue', edgecolor='white', alpha=0.85)\n",
    "ax.axvline(1.0, color='red', ls='--', lw=1.5, label='w=1 (no shift)')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Estimated weight $\\\\hat{w}(x)$')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Count')\n",
    "ax.set_title(f'Weights for {MODEL_LABELS[short]} / {DS_LABELS[ds]}')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('../figures_kaggle/fig_wcp_weights.pdf', bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Weight stats — mean: {w.mean():.3f}  std: {w.std():.3f}  min: {w.min():.3f}  max: {w.max():.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'\\nStandard CP coverage:  {results[short][ds][\"standard\"][\"coverage\"]*100:.1f}%  SS: {results[short][ds][\"standard\"][\"avg_size\"]:.2f}')\n",
    "print(f'Weighted CP coverage:  {results[short][ds][\"weighted\"][\"coverage\"]*100:.1f}%  SS: {results[short][ds][\"weighted\"][\"avg_size\"]:.2f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7 — Summary table"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pivot: per-dataset averages across models\n",
    "summary_rows = []\n",
    "for ds in DATASETS:\n",
    "    cr_std_list = [results[m][ds]['standard']['coverage'] * 100 for m in MODELS if ds in results.get(m, {})]\n",
    "    cr_wcp_list = [results[m][ds]['weighted']['coverage'] * 100 for m in MODELS if ds in results.get(m, {})]\n",
    "    ss_std_list = [results[m][ds]['standard']['avg_size'] for m in MODELS if ds in results.get(m, {})]\n",
    "    ss_wcp_list = [results[m][ds]['weighted']['avg_size'] for m in MODELS if ds in results.get(m, {})]\n",
    "    summary_rows.append({\n",
    "        'Dataset':       DS_LABELS[ds],\n",
    "        'CR_std (%)':    round(np.mean(cr_std_list), 1),\n",
    "        'CR_wcp (%)':    round(np.mean(cr_wcp_list), 1),\n",
    "        'Δ CR (pp)':     round(np.mean(cr_wcp_list) - np.mean(cr_std_list), 1),\n",
    "        'SS_std':        round(np.mean(ss_std_list), 2),\n",
    "        'SS_wcp':        round(np.mean(ss_wcp_list), 2),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "summary = pd.DataFrame(summary_rows).set_index('Dataset')\n",
    "print('Average across all 5 models (target coverage = 90%)')\n",
    "summary"
   ]
  }
 ],
